            <div class="step3-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Sense of Significance</h2>
                <p>Attaining a sense of significance is a vital need for everybody.  If we don’t figure out a way to feel significant, we can start to become stagnant, we might develop poor confidence, and our wellbeing begins to deplete. </p>
                <p>Most people naturally figure out a way to develop their sense of significance, and in the case of The Explorer Archetype, they attain their significance through experiencing the world.</p>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/sun-glow.png" style="filter:none">
                <p><strong>What’s The Point In Living If You Can’t Explore?</strong></p>
                <p>You can expect an Explorer to have a long list of places they’d like to visit, and experiences they’d like to have.  Moreover, you can be sure that they’ll go all out to attain visit these places -  this is how they feel significant.</p>
                <p>When an Explorer has no sense of significance, they will feel as though they are the undead.  Normal life without a traveling or adventure goal is the worst thing that could happen to an Explorer.</p>
                <p>If Explorers don’t have an adventurous challenge ahead of them that they are either working toward or are about to experience, they will turn inwards.</p>
                <p>Depression, lethargy, apathy and even laziness can ensue.  All of which will further cut off the lifeblood of the Explorer and pull them deeper into the depths of insignificance.</p>
                <p><strong>The Unique Challenges That An Explorer Archetype Will Face When Attaining Significance.</strong></p>
                <p>In the case of the Explorer it's not so much the challenges they face in trying to attain significance because all they need to do is meet their travel and adventure goals.</p>
                <p>But the challenge lies in how they can build themselves up and find a way to feel significant if they find themselves financially or physically unable to head off on some adventure without spiraling downwards into oblivion.</p>
                <div class="prev-next">
                    <div class="container">
                        <div class="row mx-auto col-reverse">
                            <div class="col-sm-6 mx-auto">
                                <button class="btn step2-back hover f-left">2. Unique Contribution</button>
                            </div>
                            <div class="col-sm-6">
                                <button class="btn step4 hover f-right">4. Personality Traits</button>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="step4-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Personality Traits</h2>
                <p>The Explorer is the epitome of a typical adventurer who wants to go out and explore the world around him.</p>
                <p>He or she is the traveler, the travel blogger, the adrenaline junkie or that friend that you might have who always knows the good spots to go eat or be entertained.</p>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/floral.png">
                <p>If you are friends with an Explorer and you let them lead the way when it comes to entertainment and adventures, you’ll be sure to have a good and in some cases wild time.</p>
                <p><strong>Exploring Is Everything To The Explorer</strong></p>
                <p>You may think that the Explorer is an archetype who indulges in their hobby - the love of travel and adventure, but to an Explorer, there is so much more to it than that.</p>
                <p>The Explorer experience’s all aspects of life through their adventures - to them, this is how life should be.  So where other archetypes might work on their career progression, how they give or create, or even on how they create structure in their life, the Explorer will be living their life through their adventures.</p>
                <p>It’s how they give, evolve, rest, create and find sense in the world. </p>
                <p>This is why an Explorer can make themselves feel settled and at home no matter where they are or what situation they find themselves in. </p>
                <p><strong>Most Of The Explorer’s ‘Missions’ Are Meticulously Planned</strong></p>
                <p>When the Explorer goes off on his or her travels, as much as most might think that they’d be happy to ‘wing it’ they are mistaken. An Explorer carefully considers where he or she is heading, what they want to experience when they get there and their itinerary.</p>
                <p>When Explorers are planning their adventures, they’ll always be doing so with the intention of learning more about themselves and the world that surrounds them (through their experiences). </p>
                <p><strong>Goal Oriented</strong></p>
                <p>Because of the Explorers ability to plan something and then take action, they are confident and talented at setting up and achieving goals.  You can consider an Explorer to be highly goal-oriented.</p>
                <p>However, if the goal put before them doesn’t inspire the Explorers adventurous heart, they will be likely to have no desire to work on it (even if it’s an important goal).</p>
                <p><strong>Insatiable Thirst For Knowledge Through Experience</strong></p>
                <p>Explorers are highly curious about pretty much any experience in the world that they don’t know about or haven’t tried out yet.  If the Explorers curious nature takes them to random places or experiences that they’ve never been interested in before - if it’s new they’ll try it at least once.</p>
                <p>It’s this thirst for knowledge that makes an Explorer very interesting to be around with. They will be abundant in tales of the unexpected and stories of their travels that will delight, horrify or inspire those around them.</p>
                <p><strong>Fear Of Commitment</strong></p>
                <p>But there is one problem, the Explorer finds it difficult to commit on a deep level to anything or anyone.  They feel too stifled or tied down when they commit which is in dire contrast to their need to be free and is a topic that we will discuss further on in this report.</p>
                <p><strong>Why Do We Hide Ourselves Even From Ourselves?</strong></p>
                <p>Every person has a hidden side, Jung calls it a shadow aspect, and it’s discussed in great detail in the Premium Archetype Reports.  There is a hidden side or an unconscious world (to be more precise) that we experience internally, but we don’t, or can't show or express this existence outwardly.  </p>
                <p>There’s also a hidden part of us that remains unconscious even to ourselves too.  </p>
                <p>When we start to uncover these ‘hidden’ aspects of our ‘self,’ we begin to learn about what is really driving us.  We discover the reasons why we do the things we do (or don’t do the things that we want to do, or should do).  This gives us the opportunity to start to consciously reconcile these hidden aspects so that we can achieve our deepest desires, or reach our fullest potential.  </p>
                <p>In the case of The Explorer, their hidden personality traits often lie in understanding the reasons why commitment is so intimidating to them - so that they can learn more about what is driving them.</p>
                <p>When they can understand the hidden aspects of their ‘self’ that have a significant influence on them, they can learn how to reconcile these aspects and enable themselves to take a balanced outlook on their life and how they live it.</p>
                <p>Most driving factors in an Explorers psyche will originate from deep limiting beliefs that are pushing their ideas forward into their life and have a huge influence on how you perceive the world.</p>
                <p>In general, these factors are bringing the lack of balance in the Explorers psyche to their attention so that they can realize that there is something wrong (or unbalanced) and correct that - thus enabling the Explorer to live their best life. </p>
                <p>In balancing these aspects of the Explorer’s psyche, it doesn’t mean that they will lose their unique gifts of curiosity and intrigue that make them stand out from the crowd. </p>
                <p>Instead, they’ll probably unlock their potential to explore and attain liberation on a much deeper and profound level - thus improving all aspects of their life, including their psyche.</p>
                <p><strong>Commitment Is the Explorer’s Nemesis</strong></p>
                <p>Explorers cannot stand coomitment. And while most Explorers consciously realize this about themselves, they may not understand the reasons why commitment is so off-putting to them.</p>
                <p>Unfortunately for the Explorer though, they’ll almost definitely overlook how their lack of commitment limits their opportunity to explore.</p>
                <p>Most Explorers are so focused on exploring places and things that are outside of themselves.</p>
                <p>They often take for granted the ways that we can enhance our sense of exploration or the depths of exploration that can occur when we start to work on discovering ourselves through commitment, self-reflection, discipline, and relationships.</p>
                <p>It would be surprising if any Explorers out there had realized that they might have a conflict of interest in their psyche that might jeopardize their experience of life and also causes them only to explore a small percentage of what they are capable of exploring.</p>
                <p><strong>The Secret Lies In Self Discovery</strong></p>
                <p>While an Explorer prides themselves on their adventures and worldly ways they will often remain limited when it comes to what they have discovered about themselves - and also limited in the depth of exploration they experience. </p>
                <p>For example, they may never commit enough in a relationship to enjoy the wonders of exploring the world with someone, while also learning and growing internally and intimately through the relationship they experience with a significant other - which means that the Explorer really does only explore one facet of their multifaceted self. </p>
                <p>If the Explorer were to realize their limitations and consider this notion carefully, they may find that along with their external adventures that they could even remove some of the mundane aspects of life by using that time to explore their internal world simultaneously.</p>
                <p>Self-discovery would help the Explorer grow immensely and would lead to richer experiences in life.</p>
                <p>It would also protect the Explorer if they were to ever find themselves in a situation where they cannot physically explore anymore – because their identity and sense of self will not be based solely on one facet of themselves.</p>
                <p><strong>A Conflict Of Interest</strong></p>
                <p>Some Explorers might find themselves experiencing a conflict of interest in the way that they think or experience the world.  They might want to experience a long lasting and serious committed relationship, but they cannot stand the commitment factor and so miss out on any opportunities for a committed relationship. </p>
                <p>It’s impossible to achieve growth in this situation because the Explorer is caught in a bit of a catch-22.  One need cancels out the other need, and then only one need is met, leaving the Explorer to desire the other in the shadows of their soul. </p>
                <p>This conflict of interest is easily reconciled by undertaking shadow work and starting to explore the depths of your soul so that you might connect the dots and find compromises.  It will also assist the Explorer in being able to consciously build new habits and slowly create the life they might have imagined.  This will lead to a life where the Explorer explores, travels AND has an intimate, committed relationship with a significant other.  </p>
